-# .taskorchestrator/config.yaml
-#
-# Dopemux task-orchestrator schema configuration (Option A: soft gates,
-# broad coverage via traits composability).
-#
-# Authority: ADR docs/90-adr/adr-task-orchestrator-claude-surface-integration.md
-#            ADR docs/90-adr/adr-task-orchestrator-as-workflow-authority.md (accepted)
-#            AGENTS.md §5 (PAL chains), §6 (boundaries + contract-sensitive surfaces), §9 (proof and finality)
-#
-# Implementation plan: ~/.claude/plans/on-a-new-branch-sleepy-robin.md
-#
-# CONTRACT-SENSITIVE SURFACE per AGENTS.md §6 — schema/trait changes
-# require canonical-writer inspection and ADR linkage. Treat edits as
-# breaking-by-implication unless verified non-breaking via workflow guide §9.
-#
-# Matching rules (workflow guide §3):
-#   1. Type-first: item.type matched directly against work_item_schemas keys.
-#   2. Tag-fallback: if no type match, item tags checked (substring match).
-#   3. Default: if no type/tag match, the `default` schema applies (defined below).
-#
-# Gate enforcement applies on advance_item triggers:
-#   - start (queue→work): required queue-phase notes must be filled
-#   - start (work→review or terminal): required work-phase notes must be filled
-#   - complete (any non-terminal → terminal): all required notes across all phases must be filled
-#   - cancel/reopen: bypasses gates
-#
-# Posture: soft gates. Most notes carry rich `description` + `guidance` +
-# `skill` but `required: false`. Only `proof-bundle` in review is `required: true`.
-# This gates `complete` (proof-bundle must be filled) without blocking
-# start/work transitions. Reversible upward: flip per-trait `required: false`
-# → `required: true` as discipline matures.
